{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.B4NonSaturatingBracket","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B4NonSaturatingBracket","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B4NonSaturatingBracket.a4_magnitude_bracketed_scope_a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B4NonSaturatingBracket.a4_magnitude_bracketed_scope_a","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4NonSaturatingBracket.lean#L153-L175","doc":"**(CAPSTONE) The det-gate magnitude is bracketed by derived constants and hit by\nnone — WALL(scope-(a)).**  For the witnessed straddle (`c_lo = z−h/2`, `c_hi = 2h`,\n`t* = 9.243/E₀`, verified numerically in `b4-nonsaturating-mstar-diagnostic.witness.json`\nto satisfy `b₄ c_lo < t* < b₄ c_hi`), the required magnitude is the *unique* interior\n`m ∈ (c_lo, c_hi)`, and neither derived endpoint reproduces `t*`.  Since the reaching `m`\ndepends on the target (an anchor-inversion = FIT) and lies strictly between the two\nnearest derived constants — matching neither — no identified categorical driver fixes it.\nThe det-gate magnitude remains open at scope-(a).  Nothing wired; `free_parameters = 0`.\n\nThis packages `required_magnitude_strictly_bracketed` + `no_endpoint_reproduces_target`\nas the honest verdict, parametrised by the (witness-supplied) straddle hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B4NonSaturatingBracket.detGate_no_endpoint_hits","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B4NonSaturatingBracket.detGate_no_endpoint_hits","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4NonSaturatingBracket.lean#L112-L149","doc":"**Det-space form.**  For a target determinant `D` strictly between `detG c_hi` and\n`detG c_lo` (with `c_lo < c_hi` physical), the required magnitude is interior to\n`(c_lo, c_hi)` and neither endpoint's determinant equals `D`.  Uses `detG_strictAnti`\n(det is strictly decreasing) to convert the determinant straddle into the `b₄` straddle\nof `required_magnitude_strictly_bracketed`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B4NonSaturatingBracket.no_endpoint_reproduces_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B4NonSaturatingBracket.no_endpoint_reproduces_target","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4NonSaturatingBracket.lean#L102-L110","doc":"**No straddling endpoint reproduces the target** (immediate corollary): under the\nsame hypotheses, `b₄ c_lo ≠ t` and `b₄ c_hi ≠ t`.  A derived constant that brackets the\ntarget cannot *equal* the required magnitude's cumulant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B4NonSaturatingBracket.required_magnitude_strictly_bracketed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B4NonSaturatingBracket.required_magnitude_strictly_bracketed","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4NonSaturatingBracket.lean#L70-L100","doc":"**The required magnitude is strictly bracketed by any two straddling constants.**\nGiven a positive target cumulant `t` and two *physical* magnitudes `c_lo < c_hi`\n(`0 < c_lo`, `5 c_hi² < 1`) whose `b₄` values straddle `t`, the unique `m` with\n`b₄ m = t` (existence from `magnitude_form_surjective`) satisfies `c_lo < m < c_hi`.\nConsequence: matching the target requires a magnitude strictly *between* the two\nconstants — neither endpoint reproduces it.  This is the structural core of the\nqou-j16x scope-(a) finding: the derived constants `z−h/2` (below) and `2h` (above)\nbracket the required `m*` but supply it themselves nowhere. ","signatureChunk":0}]}